"image are filled with black color. It happens because when compositing the "
"layers of the image, Krita drop color data of fully transparent pixels for "
"efficiency reason. To avoid this of color data loss you can either avoid "
"compositing of the image i.e. limit image to only one layer without any "
"masks or effects, or use the following method:"
msgstr ""
"一般来说，当 Krita 把图像保存为 PNG 文件时，为了提高处理效率，软件会在合并所"
"有图层时把完全透明的区域的颜色信息丢弃并替换成黑色。要想不丢失颜色信息，你要"
"么在制作图像时只使用单一图层且不使用任何蒙版或特效，要么使用下面的方法："

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:34
msgid "|mouseright| the layer in the layers docker."
msgstr "在图层面板中右键点击 |mouseright| 颜料图层。"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:36
msgid ""
"|mouseright| on the created mask and select :menuselection:`Split Alpha --> "
"Save Merged...`."
msgstr ""
"右键点击 |mouseright| 创建的蒙版并选择 :menuselection:`透明度通道操作 --> 合"
"并保存透明度` 。"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:41
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "How to save a PNG texture and keep color values in fully transparent areas"
msgid "Color channel values in transparent areas"
msgstr "如何在保存 PNG 材质时保留完全透明区域的颜色信息"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:43
msgid ""
"Krita treats all color channel values in fully transparent pixels as "
"**undefined**. Effectively, it means that Krita will try to skip writing to "
"(or reading from) a fully transparent pixel, unless it is really needed or "
"explicitly requested. That is done for optimization purposes and allows "
"Krita to speed up compositing the image by a lot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:46
msgid "Example 1: erasing pixels on the image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:48
msgid ""
"When erasing pixels with an eraser brush or when clearing a selection with :"
"menuselection:`Edit --> Clear` action, the color data **is not actually "
"cleared**. It is only the alpha channel that is zeroed, but color channels "
"are kept intact. You can see it yourself if you try to apply :menuselection:"
"`Split Alpha --> Alpha into Mask` on a layer after erasing with an eraser "
"brush on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:50
msgid ""
"To actually clear the color channels of transparent areas you need to apply "
"a :ref:`Reset Transparent Filter<reset_transparent_filter>` on the image. It "
"will zero-out all color channels of fully transparent pixels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:52
msgid ""
"Krita also has a special :ref:`Propagate Colors "
"Filter<filter_propagate_colors>`.  It fills the fully transparent areas with "
"neighboring colors instead of just zeroing them out, which might be useful "
"in some workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:55
msgid ""
"Example 2: compositing layers with color data inside fully transparent areas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:57
msgid ""
"If you have multiple layers, which have any color data inside their fully "
"transparent areas, the result of their merge **will not include this color "
"data**. The resulting pixels will be just zeroed out. Obviously, you cannot "
"blend two pixels with zero alpha, because you would have to divide by zero "
"for that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/split_alpha.rst:59
msgid ""
"For most workflows it just means that you should use :menuselection:`Split "
"Alpha --> Save Merged...` action to properly save the result of this split "
"alpha work. When exporting the result via :menuselection:`File --> Export..."
"`, a compositing operation may (or may not) happen, clearing out the "
"transparent areas."
msgstr ""
